+## Conformance Profiles
+
+### A Profile Has An Explicit Scope
+
+A deployment MUST identify the shared conformance profile it implements.
+
+The full-session profile MUST remain the default unless another profile is explicitly selected.
+
+A profile MUST identify each shared requirement it replaces by source file, section, and exact sentence.
+
+A profile MUST state the replacement guarantee or unsupported capability for each replaced requirement.
+
+A requirement without an explicit profile disposition MUST remain applicable.
+
+A profile selection MUST NOT bypass the amendment discipline for protected guarantees.
+
+The full-session profile is the existing scope. The task-runtime profile is a separately reviewed scope; its registration does not activate it, change an existing source pin or establish conformance. A profile does not rename an implementation identifier into a protocol version. The [task-runtime outcome](spec/decisions/runtime-profile/task-runtime.md) defines the change-process boundary for a proposed reduced task-oriented scope.
