+# Task Runtime Profile
+
+> Proposed shared outcome, inactive in the gate. Capitalized requirement keywords have the constitution's meanings. Each requirement is a single obligation under a stable heading. This profile describes task-level scope; concrete technology choices remain in each implementation specification.
+
+## Scope And Adoption
+
+The task-runtime profile separates an operator-controlled task system from the full-session platform. It does not claim control of every internal turn, tool call or record of a supplied executor. Existing implementations retain the full-session profile unless a complete alternative profile is explicitly selected with an immutable target.
+
+### The Task Contract Is Identified
+
+A task-runtime deployment MUST identify the immutable task contract it implements.
+
+The task contract MUST identify the task state it durably owns.
+
+The task contract MUST identify state owned only by a supplied executor.
+
+The task contract MUST identify its worker-loss and storage-loss boundaries.
+
+### Every Departure Is Accounted For
+
+A profile disposition MUST retain the original requirement identity.
+
+A replacement disposition MUST identify its replacement requirement or unsupported capability.
+
+An unresolved profile disposition MUST prevent a claim of profile conformance.
+
+A profile MUST preserve the distinction between selected behavior and implementation or execution evidence.
+
+The proposed v2 scope ledger is review input, not an approved waiver set. Retained requirements keep their strength and guards. A permission does not become an obligation to implement its optional feature. A conditional requirement remains conditional. The keyword-definition extraction anomaly is separately identified rather than represented as runtime behavior.
+
+## Compatibility And Gate Discipline
+
+The original signed assertions, stored forms, tool calls and full-session endpoints retain their identities for existing consumers. A task-runtime endpoint does not claim those wire contracts merely because it transports similar data. A non-additive change for an existing deployed consumer still requires the constitution's version and migration discipline. No existing dataset is converted by adopting a specification document.
+
+Record/profile selection, complete exact requirement dispositions, replacement references, native reporting and promotion checks need review together before activation. Registering this file with commented gate lines does not implement a profile-aware gate, fabricate a snapshot baseline or authorize deployment.
